    "answer": {
      "short": "At the origin, $x=0$ and $y=0$, so $y=kx$ becomes $0=k(0)=0$ for every value of $k$.",
      "worked": "The origin is $(0,0)$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{LHS}&=y\\\\&=0\\end{aligned}\\qquad\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{RHS}&=kx\\\\&=k(0)\\\\&=0\\end{aligned}$$\nLHS = RHS for every value of $k$, so every line of the form $y=kx$ passes through the origin.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
